{"tool_name":"sarotup","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"sarotup","home":"http://i.uestc.edu.cn/sarotup/index.html","summary":"Scan, report and exclude possible target-unrelated peptides from biopanning results.","addition_date":"2017-12-18T00:12:17Z","last_update_date":"2018-12-10T12:58:58Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool"],"version":["2.0"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:sarotup","credit":[{"typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"],"url":"http://i.uestc.edu.cn/hlab/"}],"documentation":[{"type":["General"],"url":"http://i.uestc.edu.cn/sarotup/help.html"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Protein sequence analysis","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_2479"}]}],"name":"SAROTUP","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"mbs_import","publication":[{"doi":"10.1155/2010/101932","metadata":{"abstract":"As epitope mimics, mimotopes have been widely utilized in the study of epitope prediction and the development of new diagnostics, therapeutics, and vaccines. Screening the random peptide libraries constructed with phage display or any other surface display technologies provides an efficient and convenient approach to acquire mimotopes. However, target-unrelated peptides creep into mimotopes from time to time through binding to contaminants or other components of the screening system. In this study, we present SAROTUP, a free web tool for scanning, reporting and excluding possible target-unrelated peptides from real mimotopes. Preliminary tests show that SAROTUP is efficient and capable of improving the accuracy of mimotope-based epitope mapping. It is also helpful for the development of mimotope-based diagnostics, therapeutics, and vaccines. \u00a9 2010 Jian Huang et al.","authors":[{"name":"Guo F.-B."},{"name":"Huang J."},{"name":"Li S."},{"name":"Lin H."},{"name":"Ru B."}],"citationCount":69,"date":"2010-05-06T00:00:00Z","journal":"Journal of Biomedicine and Biot